# Rust build output
/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
*.tmp
# Cargo.lock is committed: the exact dependency graph is part of the reproducible
# build, and reproducibility is the point of an integer-unit layout engine.

# cargo-fuzz build output. `fuzz/` is its own workspace and has its own .gitignore;
# these root-anchored entries keep `reuse lint` (which reads this file) in agreement
# with git about what is generated. Curated `fuzz/corpus/` seeds are committed.
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/coverage/

# cargo-mutants working output.
/mutants.out/
/mutants.out.old/
/mutants-*

# The six matrices of Appendices B through E are published only as PDF, and a PDF is
# not a source this project derives anything from (docs/adr/0009). A developer
# transcribing one fetches the file here; spec/PROVENANCE.toml records its digest, so
# `attest --digests` can prove the bytes are the ones this repository was written
# against without the PDF ever entering the history.
/spec/upstream/

# dune build output for engines/. The dune project root is the repository root (a dune
# rule cannot depend on a file above it, and the engines read spec/), so a default build
# directory lands here rather than under engines/. The Just recipes redirect it into
# /target instead, which is already ignored above and which `attest` skips when it looks
# for transcriptions outside spec/captured/ — dune copies those tables into whatever
# build directory it is given (engines/ocaml/README.md). This entry covers a bare
# `dune build`, which still writes here.
/_build/

# Racket build output for engines/racket. `raco make` writes a `compiled/` directory
# beside every source directory it touches — there is no equivalent of DUNE_BUILD_DIR to
# redirect it into /target — and `raco exe` writes the executable the conformance runner
# is handed. Neither is ever committed: the engine is built from source by
# `just build-engine-racket`, and the specification tables it embeds come from spec/ at
# compile time (engines/racket/embed.rkt).
engines/racket/**/compiled/
engines/racket/bin/

# opam local switches: engines/ocaml is where a developer is told to create one, and the
# repository root is where ocaml/setup-ocaml creates one in CI. Neither is ever committed,
# and `reuse lint` reads this file to know that.
/_opam/
/engines/ocaml/_opam/

# mise local overrides (per-developer, never committed)
/mise.local.toml
/.mise.local.toml

# Editor / OS
/.idea/
/.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.claude/
